        ],
        "explanation": "In GitHubInstallation.dispatch, when an Integration row exists but has no OrganizationIntegration, the new check reads integration.metadata[\"sender\"][\"login\"] directly. The sender is only stored in metadata when the install webhook state provides it (the conditional assignment near line 377). Integrations created before this change, or without a sender, have no \"sender\" key. For those, the lookup raises KeyError, which gives a 500 instead of the handled error page. The check is also not fail-closed in a controlled way, because the failure is an unhandled exception.",
